sentences.l:
As great as the door of a high-roofed chamber is made,
of a rich man, well fitted with bolts,
so great then on either side of him were the wings;

but behind
the horses, which the old man, following after, kept bidding on with the whip
swiftly through the town;

Then at once beneath his feet he bound his fair sandals,
immortal, golden, which used to bear him both over the water
and over the boundless earth, together with the breaths of the wind;

And when then they had driven past the great tomb of Ilus,
they stopped the mules and the horses so that they might drink
in the river;

So he spoke, and for the old man the mind was poured together, and he was terribly afraid,
and upright stood the hairs on his pliant limbs,
and he stood, in amazement;

Him I, very often, in the man-glorifying battle
with my eyes have seen, and when, driving the Argives to the ships,
he kept killing them, cutting them down with sharp bronze;
